2026-08-19T03:55:57.1575515Z [36;1m# "checking use of non-API entry points" check and therefore runs for[0m
2026-08-19T03:55:57.1575974Z [36;1m# every package with compiled code, read R CMD config CC, kept only the[0m
2026-08-19T03:55:57.1576415Z [36;1m# first word, and ran that. With "CC = ccache gcc" that left a bare[0m
2026-08-19T03:55:57.1576858Z [36;1m# "ccache", and the check died with "ccache: invalid option -- 'E'".[0m
2026-08-19T03:55:57.1577360Z [36;1m# https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/commit/ca19f35240517186ed447e773ee67b55e207cf27[0m
2026-08-19T03:55:57.1577830Z [36;1m# https://bugs.r-project.org/show_bug.cgi?id=19130[0m
2026-08-19T03:55:57.1578247Z [36;1m# Upstream has since dropped the truncation again, so the prefix works[0m
